  "description": "Distributed rendering via Blender CLI and ffmpeg for .blend scene blobs, bootstrap typed-scene inputs, stills, tiled stills with overlap-aware tile options, runtime diagnostics, unified/frame/video/tiled preflight validation, frame sequences, and MP4 output. Persistent-batch frame distribution renders a node's whole contiguous frame chunk in a single Blender process via the command-line animation render (scene loaded once, GUI-free / macOS-safe) with per-engine chunk sizing; tiled stills render per-tile.",
